To determine how many hash browns can be made from 96 potatoes, we start by finding out how many hash browns can be made from one potato. We know that 6 potatoes make 36 hash browns. Therefore, we can calculate the number of hash browns per potato as follows:

\[
\text{Number of hash browns per potato} = \frac{36 \text{ hash browns}}{6 \text{ potatoes}} = 6 \text{ hash browns per potato}
\]

Now that we know each potato can make 6 hash browns, we can find out how many hash browns can be made from 96 potatoes by multiplying the number of potatoes by the number of hash browns per potato:

\[
\text{Number of hash browns from 96 potatoes} = 96 \text{ potatoes} \times 6 \text{ hash browns per potato} = 576 \text{ hash browns}
\]

Therefore, the final answer is:

\boxed{576}
